file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived_confi
    > dential/5%-sample/h2_dataset.dta saved

.         
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * FILTERS *
.  
. *We include only families with 1-2 children. If participants had children dur
> ing our included panel years, this was reflected in sumkids but not biokids, 
> so we use sumkids as our basis for exclusion.
. drop if sumkids>2 | sumkids==0
(17,141 observations deleted)

. 
. *We include data limited to the years 2000 to 2020.
. drop if syear<2000 | syear>2020
(0 observations deleted)

. 
. *We include only responses from individuals over the age of 18.
. drop if bioage <18
(3,956 observations deleted)

. 
. *We include only Computer-Assisted Personal Interviews (CAPI) to avoid experi
> menter effects
. drop if pgmode!=140
(7,651 observations deleted)

.         
.         
. * GENERATE VARIABLES *
. *Tidy Control Variables
. rename bioage Age

. rename sex Male

. gen Income = pglabgro if pglabgro>=0
(2,712 missing values generated)

. replace Income = Income + pgsndjob if pgsndjob>0
(127 real changes made)

. replace pgnation = . if pgnation==-1
(1 real change made, 1 to missing)

. rename pgnation Nationality

. gen Partner_In_House = 1 if pld0133==1
(5,747 missing values generated)

. replace Partner_In_House = 0 if pld0133==2
(302 real changes made)

. replace Partner_In_House = 0 if pld0133==-2  
(5,071 real changes made)

. 
. 
. *Dependant variable
. *Our dependent variable will be a measure of political leaning -- "On the far
>  left" (0) to "Far right" (10)
. rename plh0004 Political_Leaning

. drop if Political_Leaning <0
(5,372 observations deleted)

. 
. *Independant variables
. *We create a binary variable which takes the value 1 if a respondent answers 
> to one or more of the kidsex variables that the sex of their child is 'Female
> ' and '0' otherwise.
. gen At_least_One_Daughter = 0

. foreach var of varlist kidsex01-kidsex02 {
  2.     replace At_least_One_Daughter = 1 if `var' == 2
  3. }
(486 real changes made)
(222 real changes made)

. 
. *We also consider a pre (0) and post (1) treatment dummy coded as 0 before re
> spondents have a daughter and 1 after respondents have a daughter
. //gen After_Having_Daughter = 0
. //replace After_Having_Daughter = 1 if kidsex01==2 & (kidgeb01<=syear|syear<2
> 000)
. //replace After_Having_Daughter = 1 if kidsex02==2 & kidgeb02<=syear
. 
. *To use the Callaway & Sant'Anna (2021) method of staggered DiD as a robustne
> ss check we also generate a variable for the first year respondents had a dau
> ghter
. //gen First_Year_Daughter = .
. //replace First_Year_Daughter = kidgeb01 if kidsex01==2 & kidgeb01>2000
. //replace First_Year_Daughter = kidgeb02 if kidsex02==2 & kidsex01!=2 & kidge
> b02>2000
. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 *
. *To test our second hypothesis that having daughters leads to more left-leani
> ng political preferences, we conduct a staggered difference-in-difference est
> imation with time (syear) and individual-level (pid) fixed effects and cluste
> red standard errors, of self-reported political leaning (Political_Leaning) o
> n the dummy for having a daughter or not (At_least_One_Daughter), a dummy for
>  pre and post having the first daughter (After_Having_Daughter) and an intera
> ction term of the two dummies (At_least_One_Daughter x After_Having_Daughter)
> .
. //reghdfe Political_Leaning i.At_least_One_Daughter##i.After_Having_Daughter,
>  absorb(pid syear) vce(cluster pid)
. //reghdfe Political_Leaning i.At_least_One_Daughter##i.After_Having_Daughter 
> Age Male Income i.Nationality Partner_In_House, absorb(pid syear) vce(cluster
>  pid)
. 
. // For robustness we also conduct a staggered diff in diff using the Callaway
>  & Sant'Anna (2021) method to account for treatment effect heterogeneity
. //csdid Political_Leaning At_least_One_Daughter, ivar(pid) time(syear) gvar(F
> irst_Year_Daughter) method(dripw) vce(cluster pid)
. //csdid Political_Leaning At_least_One_Daughter Age Male Income i.Nationality
>  Partner_In_House, ivar(pid) time(syear) gvar(First_Year_Daughter) method(dri
> pw) vce(cluster pid)
. 
. //Cross-sectional analysis conducted rather than panel to make results compar
> able with data used for H1 and H4
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 - CROSS-SECTIONAL*
. // 2019 selected as year for cross-sectional analysis since it has the greate
> st number of observations and 2018 did not have available data after our data
>  exclusions to make it directly comparable with the other hypotheses
. reg Political_Leaning At_least_One_Daughter if syear==2019

